{"format_version":1,"id":"18cfaea11d5c5d78695bf5b56fb443728894bdcda97f5282","commits":["39aac9d13cdd11dc138ee9330d7794e2e7bacc9f"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**`monorepo mirror --dry-run` renders a plan again.** The preview used to stop at step 1 with \"branched on unsettled value\" because observation's `git subtree split` and inspection clone were recorded instead of run; both are now allowlisted observes, and the plan no longer advertises scratch directories no apply would create.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":1,"id":"18cfaea2d424f8c7de3b8b174c054dfb81333b9fab3183c4","commits":["d5fefb7158b570035c4efcc1a15de7fa143fc0c7"],"user_facing":false}
{"format_version":1,"id":"18cfaee1f7cd388a76736c5e91cd4f21a5f7eb398e003414","commits":["43c3747fe87e85e2801ceeec4600f4dd25accd66"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Ancestry checks no longer trust a shallow repository's \"no\".** With both commits present but the connecting history truncated by a shallow fetch, git answers \"not an ancestor\" to a question it cannot follow to the end; rlsbl now treats that as undetermined, so the mirror tripwire, the release's CI-verified candidate check and `release resume` refuse instead of acting on a wrong answer.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":1,"id":"18cfaf3e8b8a3ff505af2e80e87d47bbba40b54e29c42726","commits":["18ef91cd33bf6ab2bd0df4aaf6e5f2fa2c590da9"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**`monorepo mirror` no longer reports missing objects as a contract violation.** When git cannot trace the mirror's history back to a split-lineage commit because the objects were pruned or never fetched, the reconciler now refuses with a distinct `lineage-undetermined` verdict that names the unanswerable check and points at fetching or deepening, instead of accusing the operator of authoring on the mirror.","type":"fix"}
